 <longdesc><para unique="1045948">This instruction performs a complex multiply operation. There are normal and complex conjugate forms of the oper&#173;ation. The masking for this operation is done on 32-bit quantities representing a pair of FP16 values.</para>
  <para unique="1045949">Bits 127:32 of the destination operand are copied from the corresponding bits of the first source operand. Bits MAXVL-1:128 of the destination operand are zeroed. The low FP16 element of the destination is updated according to the writemask.</para>
  <para unique="1045950">Rounding is performed at every FMA (fused multiply and add) boundary. Execution occurs as if all MXCSR excep&#173;tions are masked. MXCSR status bits are updated to reflect exceptional conditions.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1045952">VFCMULCSH dest{k1}, src1, src2 (AVX512)</title>
   <programlisting>KL := VL / 32
IF k1[0] or *no writemask*:
	tmp.fp16[0] := src1.fp16[0] * src2.fp16[0]
	tmp.fp16[1] := src1.fp16[1] * src2.fp16[0]
	// conjugate version subtracts odd final term
	dest.fp16[0] := tmp.fp16[0] + src1.fp16[1] * src2.fp16[1]
	dest.fp16[1] := tmp.fp16[1] - src1.fp16[0] * src2.fp16[1]
ELSE IF *zeroing*:
	dest.fp16[0] := 0
	dest.fp16[1] := 0
DEST[127:32] := src1[127:32] // copy upper part of src1
DEST[MAXVL-1:128] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1045969">VFMULCSH dest{k1}, src1, src2 (AVX512)</title>
   <programlisting>KL := VL / 32
IF k1[0] or *no writemask*:
	// non-conjugate version subtracts last even term
	tmp.fp16[0] := src1.fp16[0] * src2.fp16[0]
	tmp.fp16[1] := src1.fp16[1] * src2.fp16[0]
	dest.fp16[0] := tmp.fp16[0] - src1.fp16[1] * src2.fp16[1]
	dest.fp16[1] := tmp.fp16[1] + src1.fp16[0] * src2.fp16[1]
ELSE IF *zeroing*:
	dest.fp16[0] := 0
	dest.fp16[1] := 0
DEST[127:32] := src1[127:32] // copy upper part of src1
DEST[MAXVL-1:128] := 0</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
